===== /candidate/PROOF.md =====
     1	VALIDATED
     2	
     3	## What is proven
     4	
     5	Under the supplied MPY semantics, for every K string value `str(TEXT)` with
     6	`TEXT:IntSeq`, loading the exact translated `remove_vowels` definition and
     7	calling `remove_vowels(str(TEXT))` reaches
     8	`str(removeVowelsFrom(TEXT, .IntSeq))`.
     9	
    10	`removeVowelsFrom` is a stable left-to-right filter: it drops a code exactly
    11	when the fixed-semantics singleton-string membership predicate says that code
    12	occurs in `aeiouAEIOU`, and otherwise appends the code to the accumulator.
    13	Thus the returned string contains the input characters in order with lowercase
    14	and uppercase English vowels removed.
    15	
    16	This is a partial-correctness reachability theorem. The entry claim also
    17	observes the final operational state: environment `0`, the exact module
    18	function binding, scope location `1`, empty heap, heap location `0`, empty call
    19	stack, `noRet`, `NoExc`, and exit code `0`. The loop-local `char` value is
    20	existential only in the auxiliary loop claim and is destroyed when the
    21	function frame is popped.
    22	
    23	## Formal claims
    24	
    25	`SPEC.loop-invariant` states that, at the real `#loop` head, a local result
    26	`str(ACC)` and remaining iterator `str(REST)` finish with result
    27	`str(removeVowelsFrom(REST, ACC))`. It is parameterized over the input binding,
    28	current loop-character binding, environment location, parent, other scopes,
    29	continuation, and all other configuration cells.
    30	
    31	Its obligations are:
    32	
    33	- Base: `.IntSeq` leaves the accumulator unchanged.
    34	- Vowel step: fixed execution binds the one-character string, takes the
    35	  false `not in` branch, and the summary drops the same code.
    36	- Non-vowel step: fixed execution performs the real `AugAssign` and
    37	  `seqConcat`; the summary makes the identical accumulator update.
    38	- Circular step: the fixed `#loopLbl` reconstruction matches the same
    39	  `#loop` claim over the remaining `IntSeq`.
    40	
    41	`SPEC.remove-vowels` starts from the complete initial MPY configuration,
    42	executes `#loadAll` on the exact `solution.mpy` function body, performs ordinary
    43	name lookup, argument evaluation and binding, executes the loop, returns its
    44	value, pops the frame, and reaches the result and final state above.
    45	
    46	There is no input guard: the formal domain is every `str(TEXT)` represented by
    47	the supplied semantics.
    48	
    49	## Proof-extension inventory
    50	
    51	### `removeVowelsFrom`
    52	
    53	- Extension: the `[function, total]` symbol and its three rules in
    54	  `verification.k`; the two constructor-step equations are also marked
    55	  `[simplification]`.
    56	- Class: definitional summary.
    57	- Semantic role: names the mathematical output; it never matches `<k>` and
    58	  never replaces Python execution.
    59	- Domain: all pairs `(REST:IntSeq, ACC:IntSeq)`.
    60	- Matched context: only a `removeVowelsFrom` term. It has no continuation,
    61	  binding, control-stack, or configuration-cell match.
    62	- Justification scope: the empty case and both complementary outcomes of
    63	  `strContains(iCons(C, .IntSeq), VOWEL_CODES)`, where
    64	  `VOWEL_CODES = [97,101,105,111,117,65,69,73,79,85]`.
    65	- Context containment: the equations have no operational context, so their
    66	  match domain equals their justification domain.
    67	- State footprint: none.
    68	- Value influence: the loop claim's final `result` binding and the entry
    69	  claim's returned value.
    70	- Value justification: base returns `ACC`; a vowel recurses without changing
    71	  it; a non-vowel recurses with
    72	  `seqConcat(ACC, iCons(C, .IntSeq))`.
    73	- Logical checks: the empty/constructor shapes are disjoint; the two
    74	  constructor guards are exact Boolean complements; together they cover every
    75	  constructor case; recursion descends structurally on `REST`. The
    76	  `[simplification]` attributes assert the same equations and add no broader
    77	  fact.
    78	- Dependents: `SPEC.loop-invariant`, `SPEC.remove-vowels`, and both validation
    79	  probes.
    80	- Control validation: not applicable because no operational term is matched.
    81	- Value validation: universally connected to actual loop execution by
    82	  `SPEC.loop-invariant`; the complete entry theorem then connects the exact
    83	  function call to the summary. The false-result and body-mutation probes were
    84	  both rejected.
    85	
    86	### `SPEC.loop-invariant`
    87	
    88	- Extension: the reachability circularity over the exact fixed-semantics
    89	  `#loop` term.
    90	- Class: derived lemma (auxiliary execution claim).
    91	- Semantic role: proves and summarizes repeated fixed-semantics execution; it
    92	  is not an unproved operational rewrite.
    93	- Domain and matched context: all `REST`, `ACC`, input and old-character code
    94	  sequences, all environment locations and parents, every framed continuation,
    95	  other scopes, and all automatically framed configuration cells, with an
    96	  exact three-binding local scope for `text`, `result`, and `char`.
    97	- Justification scope: identical to the claimed match domain; `kprove` proves
    98	  the claim universally rather than assuming a narrower trailing computation.
    99	- Context containment: the claim itself quantifies over the framed
   100	  continuation and omitted cells. Its body has no `return`, `break`,
   101	  `continue`, exception, allocation, output, or other abrupt effect.
   102	- State footprint: reads `env` and the local scope; preserves `text`; updates
   103	  `result` and `char`; frames other scopes and runtime cells; preserves the
   104	  active continuation.
   105	- Value influence and justification: determines the local `result` by the
   106	  exhaustive equations above. The final `char` is deliberately unconstrained
   107	  because it is unobservable after frame pop.
   108	- Dependents: `SPEC.remove-vowels`.
   109	- Validation: the complete two-claim proof is `#Top`; changing the program
   110	  body to always return `""` makes the consonant witness `"b"` fail.
   111	
   112	### Other audited constructs
   113	
   114	There are no proof-local ordinary `<k>` rewrites, priority rules, operational
